   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 10 · New pose or camera angle from a reference (FLUX.3 Klein)\n**Use:** load 1–2 references → describe the scene, name them **&lt;ref_image_0&gt;** and **&lt;ref_image_1&gt;** (exactly like that)\n→ Run → `S6/ref_klein_*.png`. Distilled Klein, 16 steps, cfg 1 (template). \n**When:** the person / place should move, sit, turn, be seen from another side. Klein re-stages more naturally than Qwen 2.1, which\ncopies the reference's pose. Faces and small details (logos, embroidery) come out a little looser — for maximum likeness use\n`10_ref_qwen21`. Write the result, not the change (\"The woman from <ref_image_0> sits …\").\n\n| Reference | Use | Why (series 6, 14 refs × 3 scenes) |\n|---|---|---|\n| object / product | **10_ref_product_krea** or 10_ref_qwen21 | emblem, buckle, stitching survive (DINOv2 bag 0.87 / 0.85) |\n| garment (print, embroidery) | **10_ref_qwen21** | koi embroidery + lemon print closest |\n| face / whole character | **10_ref_qwen21** | ArcFace 0.81–0.92 from ONE photo (our Maren LoRA: 0.55) — but it copies the photo's frontal pose |\n| new pose / new camera angle | **10_ref_klein** | re-stages naturally (sits, turns, walks); details a bit looser |\n| art style / film look | **10_ref_qwen21** | gouache, risograph, Cinestill look on new content |\n| place | 10_ref_qwen21 (same view) · 10_ref_klein (other viewpoint) | Qwen keeps the exact room, Klein can turn the camera |\n| palette / light only | **10_ref_style_krea** | Qwen and Qwen-Edit 2511 paste the reference picture as the background |\n| 2–3 references at once | **10_ref_qwen21**, toggles 2nd / 3rd | face + jacket + café all kept |"
   ]
  },
